think Earlier this round I found 78 guards declaring no tier and decided 16 of them. The other 62 still default to lap silently, which is the same latent fault at smaller scale, and leaving it would mean rediscovering it.
think Chose to report rather than refuse. A roster that refused on a missing field would red on 62 guards at once, and a wall that reds on ordinary work is a wall somebody turns off. The count is a ratchet that only falls, seated at its true reading of 62, and a hand deciding one on touch lowers it.
obs The whole fault is one line: t=${tier:-lap}. A default written for convenience became a decision nobody made, 78 times, and the roster reported the result as tier_lap without distinguishing chosen from inherited.
obs The scan's verdict reads roster_broken from a receipt recorded at 20260905.161559, before this round fixed waymark_rung_drift. Run live that witness is GREEN at 17,212 against a ceiling of 17,212. A receipt is a record of a past pass, not a reading of the tree, and I have now mistaken one for the other twice today.
loom tiers lap=114 cadence=46 undeclared=62 ceiling=62
